# Base URL the compiled SDK web bundle (flutter.js, main.dart.js, assets/)
# is served from. This file is Vite's mode-independent default -- loaded by
# both `npm run dev` and `npm run build` -- and points at the CDN, so a
# `build` output (what a partner would actually deploy) matches what
# real hosts load in production. `npm run dev` overrides this to the local
# `/build_web/` symlink instead: see `.env.development`, and Vite's own env
# file docs (https://vite.dev/guide/env-and-mode) for the precedence rules.
# CDN mode assumes the bundle hosted there is the SDK's `-cdn` tarball
# variant, which fetches CanvasKit from Google's gstatic.com itself --
# CanvasKit is never served relative to this base (see ChartMount.tsx).
VITE_SDK_ASSET_BASE=https://cdn.nxtoption.com/neocharts-sdk/
